---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

/**
 * The same words the app shows under Settings → Privacy.
 * Source of truth: VastuFirst/docs/PRIVACY-POLICY.md, which itself mirrors
 * PrivacyScreen.kt. If one changes, change all three in the same week — the
 * published page and the app must never say different things.
 *
 * Google Play requires this at a public address before the listing can go live.
 */
const updated = '15 August 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — VastuFirst"
  description="VastuFirst collects nothing about you. Your homes, scores and reports stay on your phone. No account, no sign-up, no phone number."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="page">
    <Nav />
    <main id="main" class="prose-page">
      <article class="prose">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

        <p>
          These are the same words the app shows under <strong>Settings → Privacy</strong>. If one is
          ever changed, the other is changed with it in the same week.
        </p>

        <h2>Your homes stay on your phone</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you draw, every score and every report is worked out on your device and saved
          only on your device. There is no account, no sign-up and no phone number.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing about you. We do not ask for your name, email, phone number or location, and the
          app has no account to sign in to. The homes you draw, their scores and their reports are
          stored only in the app’s own private storage on your phone, where no other app can read
          them.
        </p>

        <h2>The one thing that leaves your phone</h2>
        <p>
          If you choose to have a floor plan read for you, that one picture is sent to an AI service
          to be turned into rooms, and the rooms come back. The app asks you before it does this,
          every first time, and you can turn it off again in Settings. The picture is not stored by
          us and is not linked to you — there is nothing to link it to. Drawing your home by hand
          needs no internet at all and is scored by exactly the same rules.
        </p>

        <h2>When the app crashes</h2>
        <p>
          If the app closes unexpectedly, it writes what went wrong into its own private storage and
          offers to email it to us the next time you open it. Nothing is sent unless you press send,
          and you can read the whole message first. It contains only technical detail, your phone
          model and the app version — never your homes, your scores or anything about you.
        </p>

        <h2>If you buy the full report</h2>
        <p>
          Payment is handled entirely by Google Play. We never see or store your card, and the app
          does not receive your payment details at any point. Google tells us only that this device
          has bought the report.
        </p>

        <h2>Deleting everything</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Settings → Delete all my data</strong> removes every saved home from this device
          immediately and permanently. Uninstalling the app removes everything too. Because nothing
          is stored on our side, there is nothing left for us to delete and nothing you need to ask
          us for.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>VastuFirst is not aimed at children and collects nothing from anyone, of any age.</p>

        <h2>If you join the launch list on this website</h2>
        <p>
          The email address you type into the “Notify me” box on this site is stored, together with
          the date it arrived, so that we can send you one message when the app is released. Those two
          things are all that is kept — no name, no location, no tracking of which pages you looked
          at. It is never sold or passed on, and you can ask us to delete it at any time by writing to
          the address below. The site sets no cookies and carries no analytics or advertising code.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy, or anything else:
          <a href="mailto:contact@vastufirst.com">contact@vastufirst.com</a>
        </p>

        <a class="prose__back" href="/">← Back to VastuFirst</a>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>
